A||||19||Pyric||Pioneer CD player DEH-P77DH... will it fit?||||5||
Z||000000||Pyric||11-19-2001||01:24 PM||||Any one had any experience installing the pioneer DEH-P77DH receiver in a fiero.  In is one of the GM style receivers, but I have not been able to find the dimensions for it anywhere.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DR650SE||11-19-2001||01:58 PM||||I'm not sure, I have an older CD player that is the DEH-40DH and it takes up the whole space as the stock radio did.  Its nice because it is illuminated in red and orange and matches the interior.<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-19-2001||02:13 PM||||According to Crutchfield's, this unit is a direct GM/Chrysler replacement.   <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pyric||11-19-2001||02:21 PM||||I saw that Crutchfield said if would fit, but the code said it would take modification.  Unfortunately (according to their website) Modification can be anything from splicing wires to sawing a hole in your dash.  <BR>Minor mods I can deal with, but I want it to look like it could have been original equipment.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||11-19-2001||02:41 PM||||The stereo will fit. The "modification" that it needs is the large plstic pin that supported the back of the stock radio needs to be removed. Once you pull out the stock radio, look inside the hole and you'll see it. The rest of it fit's like stock.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pyric||11-19-2001||02:45 PM||||Sweet!  I was worried about getting one because I was going to have to order it.  The info helped a lot, thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||11-19-2001||03:11 PM||||I have the DEH 76DH in my car and it does fit. The modification I had to make was removing the tiny lip on the radio/heater bezel with a dremel tool. Before I did that the removable face plate was very hard to reattach. The 77DH is a newer model but would probably have the same dimensions.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||11-19-2001||03:35 PM||||I have it. Only mod is what Orief said.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||14
Z||000008||stimpy||11-19-2001||09:13 PM||||I have it too. LOVE IT! The only mod I had to do is trim a small piece off of the bottom corners of the trim plate that goes over the holes that the radio fascia screws into. Easy money. Enjoy.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/pffp77_copy.jpg"> <BR>Yeah, I know my car is dirty.<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||camon||11-19-2001||11:29 PM||||How much is that head unit selling for?????<P>It looks sweet!<P>Looks like it could have come in the car from factory. I've been kicking around the idea of putting in a new system (to replace the stock cass.) but was worried about finding something that looked good in the car (well this looks as good as it gets)!<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||5
