Z||000014||Philphine||11-20-2001||09:56 AM||||well, now i feel dumb(er than usual). i paid $245 for the next model dowm (p-47) a couple of weeks back. nice though, and fits like everyone said. i knocked out the back brace but didn't trim the front any.<P>can i ask again while some users that have had them longer are looking, are you satisfied with the eq abilities or are you looking to use something outboard? i've played with it some but i think i want a little more eq control. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||FastFieros||11-20-2001||10:29 AM||||One I dislike about the 77 and 47 series is the rotary knob. I have had the 85 and 45 series which is older (like 3 years) but it has all buttons. When those come up on ebay they hold there resell value very well, even being an older unit. I have installed at least 10 of these Pioneers in Fieros and all have fit with no modifications to the faceplate, but 87 SE was very tight for some reason. The back support bracket will need to be removed for ease of installation, but I have seen that just bent way back out of the way and left in place.<P>loyde <A HREF="http://www.fastfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fastfieros.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pyric||11-20-2001||11:36 AM||||I was also looking at the Alpine CDAD857.  check it out on: <A HREF="http://www.competitionsound.com/cdad857.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.competitionsound.com/cdad857.html</A> <P>Anyone have experience with that one?<P><p>[This message has been edited by Pyric (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Alex4mula||11-20-2001||11:47 AM||||I too dislike the rotary volume knob. I think it changes too slowly. Also for normal hearing level I have to put it at like 35-40 level which I think is to high. Equalization is kind of limited too. Will se how it works once I set it up with my new amp.||||reg||1
Z||000018||stimpy||11-20-2001||07:53 PM||||I like the fact that it has the 3 pair of RCA jacks, including the set for the sub. I have an amp hooked to each output, and at 22, the volume is VERY VERY LOUD.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Alex4mula||11-21-2001||08:02 AM||||With the amps you can adjust the gain and is a different game. Is in stock form that I don't like it. That set of preamps is uncommon in that price range head unit. Another reason why I bought oit too.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
